  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CONSERVING THE FRONTIER ELEPHANTS: A LANDSCAPE SCALE CONSERVATION STRATEGY AND ACTION PLAN FOR ASIAN ELEPHANTS IN ARUNACHAL PRADESH, INDIA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE GOAL OF THIS PROJECT IS TO CREATE A STRATEGY AND ACTION PLAN IN COLLABORATION WITH ARUNCHAL PRADESH FOREST DEPARTMENT TO SECURE ELEPHANT HABITATS, ADDRESS SIGNIFICANT THREATS, AND PERPETUATE HEALTHY POPULATIONS OF ELEPHANTS IN THEIR NATIVE RANGE IN NORTHEASTERN INDIA. SPECIFIC OBJECTIVES ARE AS FOLLOWS: 1) ESTABLISH BASELINE INFORMATION ON POPULATION AND DEMOGRAPHIC STATUS OF ELEPHANTS, HUMAN-ELEPHANT CONFLICTS AND THREATS TO ELEPHANT HABITATS ACROSS ALL 25 ELEPHANT OCCUPIED DIVISIONS IN ARUNCHAL PRADESH 2) DEVELOP DIVISION SPECIFIC PLANS FOR SECURING ELEPHANT HABITATS AND CONNECTIVITY AND MANAGING HEC AND 3) OPERATIONALIZE THE STRATEGY AND ACTION PLAN.</narrative>
  </description>
